    "file_name": "XIN_ENG_20061128.0062.tml",
    "doc_text": "XIN_ENG_20061128.0062\n\nBAGHDAD, Nov. 28 , 2006 (Xinhua)\n\nIraqi governor survives suicide attack\n\n\n\n\nAbdul-Rahman Mustafa Fattah, governor of Iraq's northern province of Kirkuk, escaped unscathed a suicide bombing attack on Tuesday that killed one person and wounded 20 others, local police said.\n\n\"A suicide bomber wearing an explosive-belt threw himself at the convoy of Abdul-Rahman Mustafa Fattah, the governor of Kirkuk, who escaped unhurt in the center of the city,\" Brigadier Burhan, police chief of Kirkuk City told Xinhua by telephone.\n\nHowever, one civilian was killed and 20 others, including one of the governor's bodyguards, were wounded in the attack, Burhan said.",
